<title>CANADA: Canadian National Q4 profit turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Canadian National Q4 profit turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			    1995</p>
<p> Shr   Loss		C$1.96   Profit	C$0.36</p>
<p> Net   Loss	     166,000   Profit	23,000</p>
<p> Revs		   1,080,000		  962,000</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr   Profit	    C$1.67     Loss     C$13.49</p>
<p> Net   Profit	   142,000     Loss   1,085,000</p>
<p> Revs		   4,159,000		4,098,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  86,900		   81,900</p>
<p>	  (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Canadian National Railway Co. Special charges in 1996 consist of a C$365 million provision for workforce reduction and a C$16 million charge to redeem long-term debt in accordance with the company's debt reduction program. Special charges in 1995 include a writedown for asset impairment of C$1.3 billion, a provision for environmental liabilities of C$88 million, a writedown of inventory of C$14 million, C$13 million in additional legal claims and a charge in the fourth quarter of C$38 million to redeem, repurchase and defease long-term debt.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
